 ## Model Experience
 
+### Optional reservation protocol
+
+Set `reservationMode: true` to reserve estimated input plus a bounded output before
+each model dispatch. The request must have a `sessionId`. When it also sets
+`maxTokens`, that bound feeds the estimate; otherwise the estimate assumes an
+8192-token allowance and the call keeps whatever bound the caller chose, so the
+plugin never shortens a response on its own. Set `requestMaxTokens` to impose a
+hard output cap on calls that do not set their own. The stream hook never
+mutates the frozen request.
+
+The input estimate is UTF-8 JSON bytes / 3 plus a 256-token margin, including
+system prompt, messages and tool schemas. This is not a tokenizer or a billing
+guarantee: final actual usage is recorded in full even above the estimate.
+Calls without final usage hold their reservation and pause new calls for that
+scope. `missingUsage: ignore` does not override this reservation invariant.
+
+Trusted host plugins may inject `agentBudget` and use `scopeForSession`,
+`snapshot`, `reserve`, `markDispatched`, `settle`, `releaseUnsent`, `markUnknown`
+and `eventsAfter`. Operator/runtime code can allocate a `finalize` allowance
+within the total and invoke a complete async call inside
+`withPurpose(sessionId, 'finalize', callback)`. This context is not a model tool
+argument. Do not reserve a call manually and then send it through the automatic
+reservation hook: use one owner per call.
+
+The new version-2 records share the original ledger and writer lock. First
+version-2 write backs up the original ledger as `ledger.v1-backup.jsonl`.
+See `SECURITY.md` before upgrading or downgrading. Host-module tests use a
+controlled provider; remote-provider compatibility still needs a real smoke.
+
