 - `missingUsage: ignore` explicitly accepts incomplete provider accounting.
 
+## Reservation protocol upgrade
+
+Version-2 reserve/dispatch/settle/unknown/release/allocate records reuse the same
+single writer and append-only ledger. Before first v2 write, the implementation
+copies the existing v1 history to `ledger.v1-backup.jsonl`; operators must also
+back up the entire storage directory while stopped. The original 0.4.0 reader
+rejects v2 versions. Never strip v2 lines to make an old writer start: doing so
+loses obligations and can grant already-consumed credit again.
+
+Downgrade only after stopping all writers, settling/reconciling outstanding
+calls, preserving the full new history, and explicitly restoring a verified
+compatible backup. A backup predates subsequent consumption; reconcile that
+consumption before resuming old software. Do not restore a backup as a way to
+reset budget during task recovery.
+
+Dispatch intent is durable before sending a provider request. On restart it
+becomes unknown, retains its reservation, and blocks new model calls until
+authoritative usage is settled. A request that may have reached the provider
+cannot be released as unsent. The process writer lock still requires confirming
+that its recorded PID is dead before removing a stale lease.
+
+For local process-crash recovery, use the explicit checked command:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/recover-writer-lock.mjs --dir <storage-directory> --expected-pid <recorded-pid>
+```
+
+It requires a matching regular lock file and an ESRCH liveness result before
+removing that lock. EPERM, a live/reused PID, malformed identity and a concurrent
+recovery guard all fail closed. The command never modifies ledger or index
+contents. This is for a local machine/filesystem only; PID checks do not prove
+ownership on shared network storage or across containers. Interrupted recovery
+guards require offline inspection, and there must be no concurrent manual lock
+deletion. Successful lock recovery still leaves dispatched usage unknown until
+authoritative settlement; it does not make a budget available by itself.
+
+The service is trusted host code, not an authorization boundary against hostile
+plugins. Never register budget mutation or `withPurpose` as model-callable tools.
+
 ## Reporting
 
 Report reproducible security issues privately to the repository maintainer
