@@ -177,3 +177,50 @@ numeric limits, synchronizes server updates, and ignores stale fetch results.
 - Verified against DSH `0.1.0-rc.6`; when upgrading DSH, re-check the
   `llm/stream` hook signature, the `agent/request-error` payload shape, and the
   `ctx.agents` runtime ownership API.
+
+## Optional version-2 reservation protocol
+
+The preceding sample-based admission remains the default. This unreleased
+extension provides `ctx.get('agentBudget')` and enables automatic reservations
+with `reservationMode: true`. It retains the same JSONL owner and writer lock.
+
+The service offers scope resolution, snapshot, reserve, markDispatched, settle,
+releaseUnsent, markUnknown, eventsAfter, allocate and trusted withPurpose.
+Reserve atomically checks global and work/finalize capacity before a durable
+append; the first v2 append takes a v1 history backup. Model calls have one
+accounting owner. Automatic stream mode does not emit legacy samples, and
+manual callers must not reserve the same automatic call a second time.
+
+State transitions are reserved -> dispatched -> settled, with reserved ->
+released_unsent and dispatched -> unknown -> settled. Dispatch means a durable
+intent before sending, not an acknowledgement by the provider. Recovered
+dispatches become unknown. Unknown usage blocks new calls even if the legacy
+missingUsage option is ignore. Actual overshoot is recorded in full.
+
+The automatic estimate includes messages/system/tools UTF-8 bytes divided by
+three (rounded up), a 256-token margin and the explicit output cap. This is an
+estimate, not a tokenizer or guaranteed monetary cap. Requests lacking a
+session or output cap are rejected before dispatch. The agent/request hook can
+provide the default output cap (2048 or configured maxOutputTokens); final
+frozen llm/stream options are never mutated. Final cumulative usage is settled
+once only after stream completion; interrupted or unmetered streams remain
+unknown. Input/cache-read/cache-write/output are disjoint usage buckets.
+
+Finalize tokens are allocated within the global total. withPurpose uses a
+trusted asynchronous session context; the callback must consume the stream
+within that context. A model-supplied field cannot select finalize credit.
+Runtime policy separately restricts which finalization actions are permitted.
+
+eventsAfter uses the global ledger cursor, not a per-scope index. The runtime
+can persist receipts for notification recovery but must not recreate a balance.
+Snapshots and receipts are copies; duplicate settlement with equal usage is
+idempotent and conflicting final usage is rejected. Unknown schema versions,
+bad transitions and failed persistence stop further admission.
+
+Process-lock recovery is explicit: `node scripts/recover-writer-lock.mjs --dir
+<local-storage-directory> --expected-pid <dead-pid>`. It verifies the recorded
+identity, requires ESRCH for that PID and leaves all budget history intact.
+Live, reused, inaccessible or uncertain PIDs cannot be recovered this way.
+Use only a local filesystem/process namespace and stop other recovery actions.
+An interrupted recovery guard must be inspected offline; it is not auto-deleted.
+See SECURITY.md for upgrade and downgrade constraints.
